WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:05.680
Stuntman Chad Stahelski is four years younger
than Keanu Reeves and has been performing

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.930
stunts for movies and TV since 1993.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.599
Early in his career, he stood in for Brandon
Lee for reshoots of "The Crow" after Lee was

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:15.500
accidentally killed on set.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.910
Stahelski looks a bit like the improbable
love child of Alec Baldwin and George Clooney,

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.710
but he got the job doubling for Reeves in
"The Matrix" because his boss on another project

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.019
thought the two looked alike.

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:31.920
Whatever you think of their resemblance or
lack thereof, the pair became a solid team.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.160
Stahelski doubled for Reeves again on "The
Replacements," "The Matrix Reloaded," "Constantine,"

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.430
and "Thumbsucker."

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.120
He also coordinated the martial arts stunts
for "The Matrix Revolutions."

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.665
After a long career doing the stunts himself,
Stahelski mostly works as a stunt coordinator now.

00:00:47.665 --> 00:00:50.590
However, he's also found time to occupy the
director's chair.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:56.410
He has directed Reeves in all four "John Wick"
films and has a slate of many more directing

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.819
projects in development.

